    "title": "MJF Freaks Out After AEW World Title Loss - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ryan Clark ,\n33 minutes ago\nMJF’s latest run as AEW World Champion has come to an end.\nThe main event of AEW Dynamite: Spring BreakThru saw Darby Allin challenge MJF for the title in a fast-paced showdown. Allin quickly seized momentum, overwhelming the champion and landing four Coffin Drops to pick up the win.\nREAD MORE: Darby Allin Is Your New AEW World Champion – Sting Returns\nREAD MORE: Spoiler-Free Lineup For AEW Collision Spring BreakThru\nFollowing the loss, MJF reacted on Twitter, tagging Tony Khan in his response.\nThis marked the end of MJF’s second AEW World Title reign, which began in December 2025. His clash with Allin was his eighth successful defense before ultimately dropping the championship.\nNOTE: If you have any news tips or podcast recaps that you’d like to send in for us to post (full credit will be given to you), please email me at RClarkPWS@Yahoo.com .",
